    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0369" n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.248/125</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Near
                        Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-14">July 14, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>: Co<anchor n="18" xml:id="d333-f1"/>
                    has interpreted your attached memorandum of a conversation with the British
                    Ambassador on July 8<anchor n="19" xml:id="d333-f2"/> regarding the granting of
                    further export licenses for the shipment from the United States of aircraft to
                    Iran as an instruction to terminate forthwith all such further shipments, and
                    oral instructions have already been given to revoke certain licenses issued to
                    the Curtiss-Wright Corporation authorizing the export of aircraft parts to
                    Iran.</p>
                <p>Would you please let me know whether you intended that such drastic action,
                    including a ban on the exportation of aircraft parts, should be taken without
                    further investigation of the situation existing at present in Iran.<anchor
                        n="20" xml:id="d333-f3"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d333-f1" n="18" xml:id="d333-f1-content">
                <p>Division of Controls.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d333-f2" n="19" xml:id="d333-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d333-f3" n="20" xml:id="d333-f3-content">
                <p>Marginal note: “You may wish to explore this with the British Embassy—SW”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
